{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And these are the years of the life of Ishmael, etc.</b> Rabbi Chiya bar Abba said: Why were the years of Ishmael counted? In order to reckon from them the years of Jacob from the years of Ishmael. We learn that Jacob served in the house of Ever fourteen years when he parted from his father before he came to Laban — for when Jacob parted from his father, Ishmael died, as it says ״וַיֵּלֶךְ עֵשָׂו אֶל יִשְׁמָעֵאל וגו׳״ — as is explained at the end of Megillah." "<b>And expired.</b> The term גְּוִיעָה is said only of the righteous."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:27.350369149Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}